From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: a COM server registered for the user only is started

A program installed for one user registers its COM servers under
HKCU\Software\Classes\CLSID -- Chrome's notification helper, the toast
activators of desktop programs. Windows' HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT includes those;
Wine's holds only the machine's classes, so CoCreateInstance with
CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER could not start such a server (REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG):
a click on a notification of a program that had been closed could not
start it again. When the machine has no LocalServer32 for the class, the
user's is used.

Test: test/toastactivate-gate.sh (mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_USER_LOCALSERVER).
---
--- a/dlls/combase/rpc.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/rpc.c
@@ -508,6 +508,27 @@
         hr = open_key_for_clsid(rclsid, L"LocalServer32", opposite | KEY_READ, &key);
         is_opposite = TRUE;
     }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_USER_LOCALSERVER
+    if (FAILED(hr))
+    {
+        /* Stained Glass OS: a server registered for this user only, under
+         * HKCU\Software\Classes -- as programs installed per user register
+         * theirs (Chrome's notification helper, the activators of toasts):
+         * Windows' HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT includes them, Wine's holds only the
+         * machine's classes. */
+        WCHAR path[MAX_PATH];
+
+        lstrcpyW(path, L"Software\\Classes\\CLSID\\");
+        StringFromGUID2(rclsid, path + lstrlenW(path), CHARS_IN_GUID);
+        lstrcatW(path, L"\\LocalServer32");
+        if (!RegOpenKeyExW(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, path, 0, KEY_READ, &key))
+        {
+            TRACE("%s is registered for this user\n", debugstr_guid(rclsid));
+            hr = S_OK;
+            is_opposite = FALSE;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     if (FAILED(hr))
     {
         ERR("class %s not registered\n", debugstr_guid(rclsid));
